    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_39118e619f410eb2c73c1945e0b0e7c4e475a7fe1f0cb4a684e8c36259d9fa46",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The leading non-sharpness is traced to a coarse interface: a fourth moment must export total largeness across one smooth/rough split and pays for the uncontrolled rough factor. The source's proposed repair is to insert intermediate prime bands so largeness can be transferred in smaller steps, although sharp order-one control would still demand new probabilistic estimates and better information about the rough contribution.",
