      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_67265485968da2c0ec6ed1ddfe3924fede04cbd85d18d840673ae4718865bbae",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The proof deliberately assigns unequal roles to the two arithmetic factors: the P-smooth factor carries the Euler-product barriers and is polynomialized for deterministic-to-random transfer, whereas the retained P-rough factor preserves the large-prime contribution and is reduced only to its mean square after transfer.",
