    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_8e25caed89c0f8f8c72ae6cd95c46eb483a672e858dad5f723b922de1e468cdc",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The maximum proof changes representations in stages: Cauchy localization turns an unknown peak into contour mass, a fourth-moment exceptional-set estimate routes large mass through the structured smooth factor, and derandomization turns its upper corridor plus terminal lower threshold into an approximately Gaussian path constrained to stay below a barrier and finish in a high window. The two terminal-window costs, together with the squared analytic integrand, produce the characteristic three-quarter scale.",
