    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_d620994e95c45015a59eef6a79cecc8dbff18ef121d12a5be1729975e460624b",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Derandomization proceeds by first making a simultaneous prime-block corridor reliable, then compiling that corridor into finite algebra: optimized high moments control barrier failure, smooth majorants replace hard indicators, Taylor truncation produces admissible Dirichlet polynomials, and mean-value orthogonality transfers their averages to the Steinhaus model where the imported restricted Euler-product estimate applies.",
